The pysyte.cli.streams module
=============================

    >>> from pysyte.cli import streams
    >>> assert 'streams of text from cli arguments' in streams.__doc__

    >>> import sys
    >>> from pysyte.oss import platforms

Typical usage patterns
----------------------

Parse command line args for stream handling
    >>> args = streams.parse_args('testing')
    >>> assert 'streams' in dir(args)

Set up streams
    >>> platforms.copy("He's a very naughty boy")
    >>> sys.argv.append("-")
    >>> sys.stdin = StringIO("Nobody expects the Spanish Inquisition!")
    
    >>> path_to_python = streams.__file__
    >>> sys.argv.append(path_to_python)

Can say what we want the args to be called
    >>> args = streams.parse_args(name="files")
    >>> assert path_to_python in args


We added "-" to sys.argv, so stdin was requested
    >>> assert args["stdin"] == sys.stdin

Clipboard integration was turned on too
    >>> assert 'very naughty boy' in args["cliboard"].read()
